  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Media Innovation Activity in Serbia (MIA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID&apos;s Media Innovation Activity supports independent media development in Serbia, with emphasis on increased public access to relevant and accurate information; increased competitiveness of Serbian independent media and information industry stakeholders; improved access to investment capital and development finance; and application of cutting-edge technological solutions. The activity works with a wide range of stakeholders, including but not limited to professional media, digital entrepreneurs and services providers, financial sector, and others that are critical for public access to accurate information. To counter malign foreign influences and disinformation campaigns, programs will seek to ensure the long-term sustainability of the independent media as technology rapidly evolves (e.g. Internet of Things and 5G) to gain a competitive edge. The activity will facilitate the establishment of a stand-alone investment fund (a self-sustaining entity with the participation of other donors and/or private capital) to provide sustainable, long-term investment for professional independent media and other participants in the media and information sector who are critical for public access to accurate information. The activity will also work to improve the ability of citizens to discern good information from disinformation. This activity supports the USG&apos;s priority to renew and champion democracy and human rights and the Embassy ICS Mission Objective 1.2 Accountability of Essential Democratic Institutions Strengthened; and 100% of funding goes toward CAATSA Goal 5.</narrative>
  </description>
